Z||000022||BlackDragon||08-14-2001||11:00 PM||||how about if you had it all hydrolic. you could have it opperate with a button. here is the idea (still expensive) you push a button, and the whole door moves out away from the car about 6 inches. then it could pivot up. i think it would be posible with two hydrolic shocks per door, one to puch it out, one to make it pivot. you would have to come up with a new latching mechanism though.||||reg||1
Z||000023||cadaver||08-15-2001||12:42 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MD_Fiero:<BR><B>why would the body have to be re-constructed?...come on now...maybe ur right...but maybe you arent.....i see all of these other cars....no modified body panels...with those type doors...and the doors that a delorean has....no body modifactions done..if that can be done...this should be able to be done as well.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>No those cars are not modified they are built that way from the get go. If you try to do it on a stock fiero first you will hit the roof as our windows sit under the roof not next to it or on top of it. The you will hit the rear edge of the door on the jamb. Ever look at a lambo door the back edge is slanted so it doesnt hit the body. And the doors on a delorean also have a window frame that our does not have. I am not saying it cant be done. It just cant be done very easily with modifying<P>||||reg||1
Z||000024||MD_Fiero||08-15-2001||11:07 AM||||actaully the cars i were talkin about..honda CRX...and a few others..they didnt come built like that from the "get go"...as to the lambo doors, and delorean doors...i was stating...yes "stateing" that the cars i have seen with re-done doors...are done either the way the lambo has their doors, or the delorean...i wasnt saying that the delorean or lambo's were custom done..thank you ||||reg||1
